In this subject 3rd years start with manufacturing methods using a mixture of metallurgical principles. Students then investigate the different aspects of manufacturing different metal and alloy systems including the effect of material chemistry on mechanical behaviour of materials and the influence of material manufacturing techniques and heat treatment methods on the end product quality. Finally the students examine the effects as well as other aspects of metal joining methods for the manufacturing of structural elements. In particular focus is put on different metal joining methods that are used industrially.
